1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,701
Welcome to MuniQuant.

2
00:00:02,101 --> 00:00:07,157
This walkthrough uses a separate training workspace with fictional
industrial data.

3
00:00:07,557 --> 00:00:11,973
Follow the animated cursor and pause whenever you need to enter a
form.

4
00:00:12,373 --> 00:00:17,919
The platform preserves industrial evidence, facility identities and
review decisions.

5
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:22,255
First, click Workspace access.

6
00:00:22,655 --> 00:00:27,541
Enter the write token configured for your own server, then click
Enable editing.

7
00:00:27,941 --> 00:00:33,359
The masked token shown here belongs only to this disposable local
training workspace.

8
00:00:33,759 --> 00:00:35,850
Reloading the page clears the token.

9
00:00:38,183 --> 00:00:41,661
Open Sources and evidence, then click Register source.

10
00:00:42,061 --> 00:00:45,133
Register the publisher before capturing a document.

11
00:00:45,533 --> 00:00:54,002
For practice we will create a clearly labelled synthetic source;
real work should use the actual publisher and its source URL.

12
00:00:56,317 --> 00:00:59,026
Enter the source name, publisher and URL.

13
00:00:59,426 --> 00:01:05,805
Select Synthetic as the source type and Synthetic fixture as its
access status for this exercise.

14
00:01:06,205 --> 00:01:08,957
Add a note explaining that the content is fictional.

15
00:01:09,357 --> 00:01:10,637
Click Save record.

16
00:01:12,983 --> 00:01:14,349
Click Paste evidence.

17
00:01:14,749 --> 00:01:21,191
Select the training source, enter the document title, original URL
and known publication date.

18
00:01:21,591 --> 00:01:25,495
Choose text slash HTML and paste this fictional fact sheet.

19
00:01:25,895 --> 00:01:33,447
It reports annual capacity of one hundred twenty five kilotonnes,
effective January first, twenty twenty five.

20
00:01:33,847 --> 00:01:38,050
Save record preserves the exact pasted bytes and their fingerprint.

21
00:01:40,383 --> 00:01:50,026
Open the document title to check its publisher, publication date,
retrieval time, original URL and SHA two fifty six fingerprint.

22
00:01:50,426 --> 00:01:54,117
Download exact snapshot gives you the preserved source bytes.

23
00:01:54,517 --> 00:01:57,397
Inspect the source before interpreting any numbers.

24
00:01:59,717 --> 00:02:02,618
Open Industrial assets and click Add asset.

25
00:02:03,018 --> 00:02:09,311
Enter Training Smelter as the canonical name, choose Facility,
Smelter, Norway and Aluminium.

26
00:02:09,711 --> 00:02:12,698
Enter a region and only verified aliases.

27
00:02:13,098 --> 00:02:15,125
We leave aliases empty for now.

28
00:02:15,525 --> 00:02:20,730
Save the identity once; avoid duplicate records for the same
physical facility.

29
00:02:23,050 --> 00:02:26,442
Open the facility and click Record identity evidence.

30
00:02:26,842 --> 00:02:36,698
Select the fact sheet, give an exact locator such as the heading and
first paragraph, and explain how it supports the name, geography and
facility class.

31
00:02:37,098 --> 00:02:38,378
Click Save record.

32
00:02:38,778 --> 00:02:42,533
Identity evidence is separate from a capacity observation.

33
00:02:44,850 --> 00:02:49,394
Back in Sources and evidence, click Extract value beside the fact
sheet.

34
00:02:49,794 --> 00:02:52,653
Enter Training Smelter and country code N O.

35
00:02:53,053 --> 00:02:55,634
Choose Capacity and kilotonnes per year.

36
00:02:56,034 --> 00:03:00,770
Use the source supported effective date, January first, twenty
twenty five.

37
00:03:01,170 --> 00:03:05,522
Enter annual capacity of before the number and kilotonnes after it.

38
00:03:05,922 --> 00:03:09,762
Save record runs the extraction; it does not invent a fact.

39
00:03:12,117 --> 00:03:13,845
Open Training Smelter again.

40
00:03:14,245 --> 00:03:26,149
The observation history now shows the reported value of one hundred
twenty five kilotonnes per year, normalized to one hundred twenty
five thousand tonnes per year, with its effective date.

41
00:03:26,549 --> 00:03:30,453
This exact name matched the registered identity automatically.

42
00:03:30,853 --> 00:03:33,391
Check the unit and source before proceeding.

43
00:03:35,717 --> 00:03:37,722
Open Resolution and review.

44
00:03:38,122 --> 00:03:42,666
Exact names and verified aliases can resolve deterministically.

45
00:03:43,066 --> 00:03:45,370
Similar names are only suggestions.

46
00:03:45,770 --> 00:03:50,229
This training workspace includes an unresolved Bay aluminium entry.

47
00:03:50,629 --> 00:03:57,967
Click Review candidates and compare the suggested identity with the
underlying evidence before making a decision.

48
00:04:00,317 --> 00:04:06,631
Here the available evidence cannot distinguish the candidates, so
keep Reject, no suitable match.

49
00:04:07,031 --> 00:04:09,399
Enter the reason and click Save record.

50
00:04:09,799 --> 00:04:13,725
If evidence supports a candidate, select that identity instead.

51
00:04:14,125 --> 00:04:18,093
Decisions are final and attributed to the configured curator.

52
00:04:18,493 --> 00:04:27,517
A standalone name review records a decision; accepting an extracted
candidate also creates its observation and audited alias.

53
00:04:29,850 --> 00:04:32,367
Open Data quality before exporting.

54
00:04:32,767 --> 00:04:35,327
Read each finding and its remediation.

55
00:04:35,727 --> 00:04:43,258
Our new facility has identity evidence, but the seeded example
company still lacks its own locator, producing a warning.

56
00:04:43,658 --> 00:04:46,005
Warnings remain visible in the package.

57
00:04:46,405 --> 00:04:49,967
Blocking findings prevent export and must be resolved.

58
00:04:52,317 --> 00:04:55,943
Click Verify frozen replay beside the extraction build.

59
00:04:56,343 --> 00:05:02,338
The server reruns the versioned parser against the preserved
snapshot and checks equivalent candidates.

60
00:05:02,738 --> 00:05:06,151
The confirmation here reports one equivalent candidate.

61
00:05:06,551 --> 00:05:13,911
This verifies extraction reproducibility; it does not independently
certify that the industrial claim is true.

62
00:05:16,250 --> 00:05:18,298
Click Export version one package.

63
00:05:18,698 --> 00:05:23,690
A successful validation downloads commodity evidence package dot
JSON.

64
00:05:24,090 --> 00:05:31,023
The package carries the source references, fingerprints, dates,
exact numeric values and quality findings.

65
00:05:31,423 --> 00:05:37,034
Use Download contract schema if another application needs the formal
data structure.

66
00:05:37,434 --> 00:05:40,207
This training export contains fictional data.

67
00:05:42,517 --> 00:05:50,325
For real evidence, register the actual publisher and leave access as
Review required until you have checked permitted use.

68
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:59,663
Click Review access, enter the approved exact hostnames, access
basis and retention policy, then select the justified decision.

69
00:06:00,063 --> 00:06:07,103
This form is shown for instruction only; we are not granting a real
publisher permission in this training exercise.

70
00:06:09,450 --> 00:06:13,695
After a real source has a permitted policy, click Retrieve URL.

71
00:06:14,095 --> 00:06:21,007
Choose that source, paste the exact document URL and title, and
enter a publication date only when known.

72
00:06:21,407 --> 00:06:24,138
Save record retrieves and preserves the bytes.

73
00:06:24,538 --> 00:06:30,682
Our synthetic source is deliberately absent from this permitted
source list, so we do not submit this form.

74
00:06:32,983 --> 00:06:46,338
Your routine is: register the source, preserve the document,
register the facility, link identity evidence, extract the value,
review uncertain matches, check quality, verify replay and export.

75
00:06:46,738 --> 00:06:50,258
Pause this video to copy the demonstrated training entries.

76
00:06:50,658 --> 00:06:53,645
For real work, use source supported dates and facts.

77
00:06:54,045 --> 00:06:57,991
The accompanying transcript includes the exact practice values.
